{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1tUg9DdmZeLUnM1BHVX", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with low confidence (0.4). Of the four bugs I reported, the developer confirmed one and said they could not reproduce the other three.\n\n- **Confirmed:** the Subtasks row in the sort sheet shows a \"Descending\" toggle even when it is set to \"My order\", where a direction makes no sense.\n- **Title sort Descending:** this was reported twice and not reproduced either time. With Grouping set to None, Sorting By title Descending left the list in ascending order: Buy milk, Pack for trip, Pay rent, Read docs. I saw it twice, and By due date Descending did reverse the list correctly.\n- **Note link:** \"See https://example.com/guide\" in the Read docs notes looks like plain text. It has no link styling, and tapping it just put the cursor in the field. I never saw a browser open, and I did not check whether the link works in the task list.\n\nGrouping by due date looked right: headings were \"Due Thursday\", \"Due Tuesday, November 24\", \"Due Friday, December 4\" and \"No due date\", and reversing the grouping direction worked. I did not test rotating the screen, a different date format, or the other sort options beyond title and due date."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 251, "cache_read_input_tokens": 84073, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 251}, "output_tokens": 381, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "7f572fe7-db98-46b6-8949-e8f40549baf9", "uuid": "83c7ca39-0685-45a3-a529-e836f1326e8c", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T00:39:27.140Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1tUf5D